/**
 * A stack with O(1) push, pop, and mode-query operations.
 * The "surprising" feature: constant-time MODE() — returns the most 
 * frequently occurring element currently in the stack.
 */
public class ModeStack {
    private static class Node {
        int value;
        int frequency;  // frequency of this value in current stack
        Node next;

        Node(int value, Node next) {
            this.value = value;
            this.next = next;
            this.frequency = 1;
        }
    }

    private Node top;
    private Map<Integer, Integer> valueFreq;      // value → count
    private Map<Integer, Node> freqToModeNode;    // frequency → node with that freq (mode candidate)
    private int maxFreq;

    public ModeStack() {
        this.top = null;
        this.valueFreq = new HashMap<>();
        this.freqToModeNode = new HashMap<>();
        this.maxFreq = 0;
    }

    /**
     * Push a value onto the stack. O(1).
     */
    public void push(int value) {
        // Update frequency map
        int oldFreq = valueFreq.getOrDefault(value, 0);
        int newFreq = oldFreq + 1;
        valueFreq.put(value, newFreq);

        // Update max frequency and mode tracking
        if (newFreq > maxFreq) {
            maxFreq = newFreq;
        }
        freqToModeNode.put(newFreq, new Node(value, null));

        // Push onto stack
        top = new Node(value, top);
    }

    /**
     * Pop and return the top value. O(1).
     */
    public int pop() {
        if (top == null) {
            throw new EmptyStackException();
        }

        int value = top.value;
        top = top.next;

        // Update frequency map
        int oldFreq = valueFreq.get(value);
        int newFreq = oldFreq - 1;

        if (newFreq == 0) {
            valueFreq.remove(value);
        } else {
            valueFreq.put(value, newFreq);
        }

        // Update max frequency if needed
        if (oldFreq == maxFreq && !valueFreq.values().contains(maxFreq)) {
            maxFreq--;
        }

        return value;
    }

    /**
     * Return the most frequently occurring element in the stack. O(1).
     * In case of ties, returns any element at max frequency.
     */
    public int mode() {
        if (top == null) {
            throw new EmptyStackException();
        }

        Node modeNode = freqToModeNode.get(maxFreq);
        return modeNode.value;
    }

    public boolean isEmpty() {
        return top == null;
    }
}
```

**Why this design is interesting:** Most constant-time queries track aggregates (sum, min/max via auxiliary stacks). Mode is harder—it requires tracking which value appears most often *and* maintaining that answer
